I also recently learned during a phone call with a TransUnion representative that disputes remained open and awaiting furnisher response beyond the 30-day FCRA deadline under 611 ( a ) ( 1 ) ( A ). The FCRA does not allow a bureau to exceed the deadline simply because a furnisher has not responded. After 30 days, the information becomes unverifiable by law and must be deleted. Instead, TransUnion continued reporting the items, in direct violation of the statute. 

