More recently, I received a breach notification from XXXX, a TransUnion-affiliated company, confirming that my SSN and date of birth were exposed in a major TransUnion data breach. The notice failed to state how long my data had been exposed, leaving me vulnerable with no clear timeline to protect myself. 

As a direct result of these compromises, I have experienced : Accounts opened without my consent Address variations I never used Unauthorized inquiries Joint credit accounts established without my authorization Derogatory reporting tied to identity theft Despite receiving all required documents, TransUnion refused to block the fraudulent items, failed to verify the data, ignored MOV requirements, and kept the accounts reporting after the legal deadline. 

