17922804,2025-12-03,Debt collection,Telecommunications debt,Written notification about debt,Didn't receive enough information to verify debt,"I disputed a collection account that is being reported on my credit report. 
As part of my dispute, I requested validation of the alleged debt from the collection agency, including documentation proving the debt is mine and that the agency has the legal right to collect it. 

The collection agency failed to provide any validation or documentation. 
Despite failing to validate, they continued reporting the account to the credit bureaus. 

The credit bureau verified the account without the collection agency supplying actual validation, which violates the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act ( FDCPA 809 ( b ) ) and the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA 623 ).

A furnisher can not legally report information that has not been validated when requested, and a credit bureau can not verify information without proof. 

I am requesting that the CFPB intervene and have this unvalidated account deleted from all of my credit reports. I also request a written explanation of how the account was verified without any documentation being provide",,CL Holdings LLC,LA,700XX,,Web,2025-12-03,Closed with explanation,Yes
