17993703,2025-12-01,Vehicle loan or lease,Loan,Managing the loan or lease,Billing problem,"b'To Whom It May Concern,\n\nThis letter challenges the validity of the Notice of Intent to Accelerate dated XXXX XXXX XXXX The notice is defective under Texas law and inconsistent with my Motor Vehicle Retail Installment Sales Contract XXXX XXXX XXXX  executed XXXX XXXX XXXX.\n\nYour notice lists Other Fees/Expenses: $XXXX in addition to late fees of $XXXX. That $XXXX fee is not authorized anywhere in my contract:\n\nPage 2  Itemization of Amount Financed: Lists all permissible fees at origination. No category authorizes new other fees later in the life of the loan.\n\nPage 3, Section 3 (If You Pay Late or Break Other Promises): Allows only a late charge of 5% of the scheduled payment and, if applicable, a returned check fee. No additional default fees are permitted.\n\nPage 1  Returned Check Charge: Fixed at $XXXX, not $XXXX.\n\nPage 4, Section G (Collection Costs): Only applies if an outside attorney is hired, which has not occurred, and cannot be used to add pre-acceleration fees.\n\nPage 2 also requires any other charge to be identified, with who it is paid to and for what purpose. Your notice does not state what the $XXXX is, who received it, why it was charged, or what contract provision authorizes it. A fee that cannot be traced to a contract line item is void and cannot be part of the cure amount.\n\nTexas Finance Code 348.119 and related provisions require that a cure notice state the correct, itemized amount due and include only lawful, contract-authorized charges. Because the $XXXX Other Fees/Expenses is unauthorized, unexplained, and not itemized, the cure amount in your notice is incorrect. A notice with an inaccurate or unlawful cure amount is invalid and cannot support acceleration or repossession under Texas Finance Code Chapter 348 and Texas UCC 9.611.\n\nAccordingly, Santander may not lawfully accelerate the loan, demand the full balance, report acceleration, or repossess the vehicle based on the defective XXXX XXXX XXXX  notice.\n\n\nUntil a lawful, contract-compliant notice is issued, Santander is barred from taking any enforcement action based on the XXXX XXXX XXXX notice.\n\nI reserve all rights under Texas Finance Code Chapter 348, Texas Business & Commerce Code 9.6019.624, the Texas Deceptive Trade Practices Act, federal consumer protection laws, and all contractual and common-law rights. Nothing in this letter waives any rights or legal claims.\n\nSincerely,XXXX XXXX",,"SANTANDER HOLDINGS USA, INC.",TX,XXXXX,,Web,2025-12-01,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes
