18210882,2025-12-22,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account information incorrect,"To Whom It May Concern, I am submitting this letter as a formal complaint regarding a collection account that has been placed on my consumer credit report without proper validation and in violation of federal consumer protection laws.

Under the Fair Debt Collection Practices Act ( FDCPA ), 15 U.S.C. 1692g, a debt collector is required to provide a written validation notice within five ( 5 ) days of the initial communication with a consumer. This notice must include the amount of the debt, the name of the original creditor, and a statement of the consumers right to dispute the debt and request validation.

I did not receive a validation notice within the required timeframe, nor was I provided with proper documentation prior to the debt being reported to the credit bureaus. Specifically, I did not receive the following documents : The Flow-Free Agreement Any Transfer or Assignment of the Debt A Bill of Sale showing ownership of the debt The Original Contract bearing my signature Additionally, I did not receive any Demand Letter or notice of intent to collect prior to this account being furnished to the credit reporting agencies.

Pursuant to the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), 15 U.S.C. 1681, consumer reporting agencies and data furnishers are required to ensure that information reported is accurate, complete, and verifiable. Reporting a collection account without first validating the debt constitutes inaccurate and unverified reporting.

Furthermore, the practice of placing a collection account on a consumers credit report without first notifying the consumer or providing validation is commonly referred to as debt parking. This practice has been identified by the CFPB as deceptive and unfair, as it deprives consumers of their right to dispute or validate the debt before credit damage occurs.

Because the alleged debt was never properly validated, never lawfully assigned with proof, and never disclosed to me prior to credit reporting, I dispute this account in its entirety and request that the CFPB investigate this matter for violations of the FDCPA and FCRA.

I respectfully request : Full validation of the alleged debt, or Immediate removal of the collection account from my credit report Thank you for your attention to this matter and for protecting consumer rights under federal law. 

